WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:56.640
I don't know why you have to be so grumpy.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.280
It's not that far out of the way.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.920
Sixteen miles each way, thirty-two miles.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.920
You don't think that's far?

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.160
Not to make somebody happy.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.760
Why do you think it's going to make the chief happy?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.760
I don't think he likes birthdays anyway, particularly his own.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.720
We lacked our gift last year.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.120
He said he liked it.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.640
Well it's not every San Francisco police officer who has his own antique inlaid serpentine

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.040
crease.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.600
That's a point I'll give you.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.680
Anyway, we ought to get him a tie, or better still, forget about it.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.040
Oh boy.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.040
Oh boy what?

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.040
Forget about birthdays.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:37.160
If you didn't have a birthday, you wouldn't be...

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.200
You wouldn't be what?

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.200
You just wouldn't be.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.200
And anyway, you wouldn't know what sign you were born under.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.200
Sign?

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.940
What sign were you born under?

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.400
It said Wesley Memorial Hospital.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.400
Why?

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.360
I'm not that kind of a sign.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:00.040
Sign of the zodiac, astrological sign.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.240
Here's my horoscope for today.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.840
You will have a dramatic surprise.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:05.920
How about that?

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.920
Now it's my turn to say oh boy.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.920
All right.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.440
Listen to this.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.840
Born leader, shrewd, decisive, commanding and warm and generous, and yet an implacable

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.760
foe of injustice.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.200
Who does that describe?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.360
Washington, Jefferson, Lincoln, and Robert T. Ironside.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.400
Not necessarily in that order.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.400
Right.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.160
But it happens to be the people born under your sign.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.160
Mine?

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.160
That's right.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:34.160
Cancer.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.160
The crab.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:03:03.920
There, that antique kettle.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:09.840
You're kidding.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.800
I certainly am not.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.120
For the chief's birthday present?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.400
He can use it as a planter.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.400
I was lucky.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.320
I only found it by accident.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.320
More of a disaster, I'd say.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.320
Shankan al-sanku.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.360
Now what does that mean?

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:33.520
It means, while you probably prefer young dishes, my taste runs to old pots.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:46.280
Try one of these.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.520
Try what you missed.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.520
I'll take that one.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:52.520
Got the permit?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.520
Sure.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.520
This expired.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:55.520
1965.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:05.760
Oh, it's a nine, 1969.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.760
I just renewed it.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.440
Listen, mister, I just got a messenger job at the bank.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.440
I need that piece.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.440
All right, all right.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:29.040
Thank you.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:46.800
Yes, miss?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.800
I'd like that kettle, please.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:48.800
Oh, it's just lovely.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.800
You got a good buy.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:59.640
Okay, pops, you too, miss.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:09.200
What are you, a grinch or something?

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.200
Gun's not even loaded.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.200
You want to push it?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.200
Chief?

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.200
The back door.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.200
Hurry.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:26.760
We got no rough patヒng possible.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:36.760
♪♪

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:46.780
♪♪

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:56.780
♪♪

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:06.800
♪♪

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:16.800
♪♪

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:26.820
♪♪

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:36.820
♪♪

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:46.840
♪♪

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:56.840
♪♪

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:06.860
♪♪

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:16.860
♪♪

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:26.880
♪♪

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:36.900
♪♪

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:37.900
Chief?

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:38.900
Don't talk, Eve.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:44.900
Young, brown hair, leather jacket.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.900
Later, Eve.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:52.900
All right, Mark.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:56.900
Don't you want to stick with her?

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.900
There's nothing we can do at the hospital right now

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.900
except get in the way.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.900
All right, you go ahead.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.900
Ed can drive me.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:17.900
-♪♪

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.900
Castle, double S, double L, first name Fred.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.900
5-4-2-1 Harrison.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:27.900
And a number, Juliet 7-8-9-3.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.900
I'll be in touch.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:30.900
How do we stand?

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.900
The neighborhood's covered from 8th to Fremont.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.900
Checking everyone in the building.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:35.900
Somebody may have seen him.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:36.900
Got a description?

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:37.900
Pretty thin.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:40.900
I'm hoping we'll get a lead from one of those guns.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:43.900
Eve thought she saw him handling one of them.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.900
What about this Fred Castle?

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:46.900
I don't know.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.900
The pad was next to the guns.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.900
Could be the name of the suspect or another customer.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:52.900
J-7-8-9-3.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.900
Some kind of a license number, I think.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.900
We're checking it out.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.900
What was Eve doing in this place?

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.900
Looking for a birthday present for you.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.900
I was right outside.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.900
If only I'd come in with her, maybe it wouldn't have happened.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:18.900
If, maybe, the world's greatest rationales wasn't your fault.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:19.900
Whose then?

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:38.900
Maybe mine.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:55.900
Officer, do you mind telling me just how long you intend keeping us here?

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:56.900
Only a few more minutes.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.900
That's what you said half an hour ago.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:02.900
Brown, there's a small mob out there.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:04.900
Why isn't someone handling it?

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:08.900
Sir, I've got some extra men coming in from the Rand Street station.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.900
How, by dog sled?

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.900
I didn't expect to see you here, sir.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.900
Any time a cop gets shot, expect me.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.900
What was Chadwick doing here?

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:23.900
Having a drink.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:24.900
The suspect showed a gun.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:26.900
Chadwick went for him, but didn't want to shoot.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:27.900
Too many people around.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.900
The killer didn't have that problem.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:30.900
Excuse me.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.900
Are you the officer in charge?

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:33.900
I'm the deputy.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:34.900
I'm the deputy.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:35.900
I'm the deputy.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:36.900
I'm the deputy.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:37.900
I'm the deputy.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:38.900
I'm the deputy.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.900
Are you the officer in charge?

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:42.900
I'd like to think so.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:46.900
This is Chief Ironside, Miss Eve Whitfield, and Paul Fulham.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.900
Miss Whitfield gave me a description of the suspect.

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.900
I had a good look at him.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.900
Whitfield.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:54.900
Any relation to Howard Whitfield?

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:55.900
He's my father.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:56.900
Do you know him?

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:57.900
In a way.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:58.900
We did business together.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.900
Oh, well.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.900
One of his banks held the pink slip on my car.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:10.900
Be with you in a minute, Miss Whitfield.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:14.900
Chief Ironside, I'm not accustomed to being treated this way.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.900
Then don't come to dives like this.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.900
Not just a minute.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.900
You're not talking to one of your criminals.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.900
Perhaps in his eyes.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.900
Would the charge be slumming, Chief?

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:27.900
This isn't exactly your kind of playground.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:32.900
I believe one of our constitutional freedoms is the right to go wherever we please.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.900
And even the rich can enjoy it.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:39.900
I trust you have tonight.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:42.900
All right, Miss Whitfield.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.900
You've described the suspect to Sergeant Brown.

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.900
Describe him to me.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.900
The man you're looking for is about Paul's height and build.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:55.900
He wore a tan sport jacket, brown slacks, brown hair, straight combed back,

00:11:55.900 --> 00:12:01.900
low forehead, rather flat features, thin mouth, and a strong chin, I thought.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.900
That's all I can be sure of.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.900
You're very observant.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:06.900
If that's all...

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:08.900
Miss Whitfield, you could do us a great favor.

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:12.900
Repeat your description to our artist down at headquarters. He can make a sketch.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:13.900
When?

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.900
Right now, while the details are still fresh in your mind.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.900
You don't ask many favors, do you, Chief Ironside?

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:24.900
I don't usually need them.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.900
Whenever you're ready.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:31.900
Thank you. My car's just outside.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:35.900
You haven't picked him up by now, you won't. He's either gotten through or he's holed up.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.900
What about the name Fred Kessel?

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.900
A couple of men are at that address now.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:43.900
Haven't heard from them yet, but that number you gave us checks out.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:44.900
Well?

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:48.900
Gun permit. Expired in 1967 in Kessel's name.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:53.900
All right. Dig into him. Hard. He can reach me at the hospital.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.900
He give you any word about Eve?

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.900
No. She's still in the emergency room.

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:02.900
I keep thinking she'll be all right. She'll fight.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:04.900
He's too stubborn to quit.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:09.900
Chief Ironside, did you see the man or did I?

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:14.900
I said that his eyes were farther apart and that there was a flatness to the bridge of his nose.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:20.900
In all the noise and confusion, people running around screaming, you can be sure about a little detail like that?

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:21.900
I am positive.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:22.900
Fix it, George.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.900
Yes, sir.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:30.900
Is this your usual police technique? Badgering your witnesses, trying to confuse them?

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.900
It helps to sift out the truth.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:36.900
I think I could find a better way.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:41.900
Probably. Don't think she couldn't.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.900
I'll get her a badge.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.900
I'll take care of that.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:56.900
A person's belongings are given to a relative or held here until such time.

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.900
I'm a friend. We work together.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:04.900
I'm sorry, but hospital regulations are very strict.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:07.900
Did you think I'd try to steal it?

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.900
No, of course not. But...

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:17.900
Well, I suppose in this case...

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:19.900
Thanks.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:47.900
Welcome.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.900
Mark, have you seen my purse? Oh, there. I knew I left it up here.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:54.900
It was hanging on the chair. I didn't see it. Knocked it off.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:57.900
Oh, that's all right. I'll take care of it.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.900
Where's the chief?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.900
Following doctor's orders. Taking his nap in my room.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.900
How did you manage that?

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.900
Just dumped him in the bed and closed the door.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:14.900
Something tells me that you're going to be the best thing that could have happened to him.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:17.900
Don't you want to check it first, Miss Whitfield?

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:18.900
What?

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:21.900
The purse. To make sure nothing's missing.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.900
Is there anything missing?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.900
No.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.900
Then why should I check it?

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.900
How long have you been here now, Mark?

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.900
Just about a week.

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:45.900
And don't you think it's about time you began to trust us?

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:49.900
Mark!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:50.900
What's happening?

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:56.900
She's still in the emergency room.

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.900
Did you reach Miss Whitfield's parents?

00:15:58.900 --> 00:15:59.900
Not yet, doctor.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.900
Keep trying. We're taking her to surgery now.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.900
How is she?

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:32.900
Critical.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:35.900
It'll be at least a couple of hours, Chief Ironside.

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.900
Now, I could call you at your office when we hear...

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.900
Thank you, but time won't go any faster there.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:51.900
All right. I'll try to keep you posted.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.900
Guess we'll move from the Harrison Street address over a year ago.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:17:02.900
The men are following up on a forwarding address.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.900
What about the prints on those guns?

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.900
No record here. Checking with Washington.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.900
Want some coffee, some sandwich?

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.900
It's going to be rough on Eve's parents.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:11.900
They should be notified personally.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:13.900
But they're not home.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.900
You imagine they've abandoned that place permanently?

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:18.900
That place?

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:20.900
No.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:22.900
Not the way I remember it.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:31.900
Not the way I remember it.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:34.900
Good afternoon, gentlemen. May I have your invitations, please?

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.900
Invitations.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:40.900
Robert T. Ironside, Chief Inspector of San Francisco Police with Sergeant Ed Brown.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.900
Police?

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:44.900
We'd like to see Miss Whitfield, please.

00:17:44.900 --> 00:18:00.900
Well, I, um... Come in.

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:04.900
If you'll wait here, please.

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:07.900
I have a feeling we should come in the service entrance.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:09.900
Junette Brown, this is a democracy.

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.900
Good afternoon, gentlemen.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.900
How good of you to come.

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:15.900
I'm Margaret Whitfield.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.900
Oh, didn't Frederick show...

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.900
Oh, well, come with me.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:20.900
Hi.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:21.900
Hi.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:22.900
Hi.

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:25.900
Hello.

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:28.900
We're very crowded, but I'm quite sure you can find seats.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:31.900
Mrs. Whitfield, I'm afraid you don't understand.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:33.900
What a lovely surprise.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.900
Good afternoon, Chief Ironside, Sergeant Brown.

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:36.900
Hello again.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:37.900
You've met my mother?

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:39.900
Yes, dear. I was just going to find room for them.

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:41.900
It's all right. I'll take care of it.

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.900
We're running short of sandwiches. Would you ask Frederick to bring the other trays in?

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:49.900
Of course. Very nice to have met you, gentlemen.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.900
Well, what can I do for you, Chief Ironside?

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.900
I'm assuming, of course, you're here to see me.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.900
I've been trying to reach you all morning, Miss Whitfield.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.900
They kept telling me that you were busy and that you'd call back.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:05.900
I'm sorry. There was so much to do this afternoon, and I had to get ready.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.900
So Mohammed came to the mountain.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:09.900
Or is it the other way around?

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.900
I'm sorry to drag you away from your party.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.900
Oh, it's really not a party. We're just having a fashion show. A benefit. Would you come in?

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:19.900
No, thanks. We really don't have the time.

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:23.900
We checked the sketch you made last night against our mug files.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.900
Came up with those three men.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:28.900
Is any one of them the man you saw?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:33.900
Yes.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.900
Which one?

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.900
What's it worth to you?

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.900
I don't understand.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.900
You want me to help you, is that right?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:42.900
Well, it's not exactly...

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:44.900
Then I think it's only fair that you help me.

00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:46.900
Us.

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:47.900
By buying a raffle ticket.

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:48.900
Miss Whitfield...

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.900
It's the least you can do.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:52.900
Anyway, you should be in sympathy with the cause.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:55.900
It's for the police, widows and orphans' aid.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:56.900
How much are they?

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:58.900
Five dollars. How many would you like?

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.900
One.

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:02.900
We'll split it.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:03.900
It's that one.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:04.900
You're sure?

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:06.900
Please, no more technique, I'm sure.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:07.900
Steve Lasko.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:08.900
Thank you.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:11.900
Excuse me, Chief Ironside. You're wanted on the telephone.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:12.900
This way, please, sir.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.900
Take care of the ticket.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.900
I'll pay you later.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.900
Thank you.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.900
Ironside.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:25.900
Bonaro, Chief.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.900
Teletype just came in from Washington.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:30.900
The prints on one of those copies are the same.

00:20:30.900 --> 00:20:34.900
The prints on one of those guns belong to Frank Sharkey.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:36.900
Wanted on the East Coast.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.900
Six counts of armed robbery.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.900
Sounds promising.

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:41.900
Put out an APB.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:42.900
In the works.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.900
We got another address on Fred Kessel.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.900
Want us to follow up?

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.900
Maybe some kind of tie-in.

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:52.900
What is it, Kessel?

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.900
1322 Ecker.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:00.900
Ecker. Apartment 5.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.900
Right, I'll send Ed over.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:06.900
Okay. I'm on my way.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:08.900
Sergeant.

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:10.900
May I see that?

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:20.900
.357 Magnum.

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:24.900
What happened to your service revolver?

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:26.900
I've been pulling around with this on the range.

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:28.900
A little more stopping power.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:31.900
And you decided this might be a good time to try it out in the field.

00:21:31.900 --> 00:21:33.900
What were you planning on stopping? A tank?

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:36.900
There's no regulation against it.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.900
On second thought, I'm coming with you.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.900
Waiting around here has got me ready to jump out of my skin.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:43.900
Chief.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.900
All right, you stay if you want.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.900
But you're a glutton for punishment.

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:51.900
And tell the ME I want a report before lunch.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:54.900
If he can't do it, I'll come down and perform the autopsy myself.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:55.900
Yes, sir.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:56.900
Chief.

00:21:56.900 --> 00:21:57.900
Chief Einstein.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.900
I've been looking all over for you.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:00.900
Good morning, Sergeant Brown.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.900
Miss Whitfield.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.900
You wanted to see me?

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:06.900
Yes. Your raffle ticket won a door prize.

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.900
I don't have to ask what it is.

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.900
The latest Paris creation.

00:22:10.900 --> 00:22:12.900
Here. Probably fits you better than me.

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:15.900
Thanks. Nice seeing you again, Miss Whitfield.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:18.900
Well, thank you for your trouble, Miss Whitfield.

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.900
Oh, no trouble at all.

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:22.900
I was coming downtown anyway.

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:24.900
Well.

00:22:31.900 --> 00:22:33.900
Would you like to come in?

00:22:40.900 --> 00:22:42.900
Really, Chief.

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:45.900
You ought to have a better office.

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:48.900
This could belong to an accountant or a professor

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:50.900
or just about anybody.

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:54.900
But a detective, especially one as important as you,

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:59.900
should have someplace so big, impersonal, scientific.

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:02.900
Someplace full of gadgets to help him find clues

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:04.900
and track down murderers.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.900
Well, I'm probably keeping you from your work.

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:10.900
You must have dozens of mysteries to solve.

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:12.900
Goodbye, Chief.

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:14.900
Miss Whitfield.

00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:16.900
Sit down.

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:26.900
You know, you didn't just come here to deliver a data report.

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:28.900
You came here to help me.

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:30.900
I'm not a detective.

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:35.900
You know, you didn't just come here to deliver a door prize.

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:39.900
I may have a big mouth, but I've also got big ears.

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:41.900
Now, come on, sit down.

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:56.900
If you want the whole truth, you didn't win any prize at all.

00:23:56.900 --> 00:24:00.900
That was the only excuse I could think of.

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:03.900
Well, I can't say I'm broken-hearted.

00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:06.900
All of a sudden, I don't know what to say.

00:24:08.900 --> 00:24:12.900
Lascoe guilty, sentenced to a gas chamber.

00:24:12.900 --> 00:24:14.900
Yes.

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:19.900
And you feel that you're going to be the executioner.

00:24:19.900 --> 00:24:22.900
I was the only witness who could identify him.

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:25.900
Plus a dozen detectives who matched his fingerprints,

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:28.900
checked the bullets from his gun, traced the money he stole,

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:31.900
backtracked his moves, all under my orders.

00:24:31.900 --> 00:24:36.900
By your definition, Miss Whitfield, I'm the executioner.

00:24:36.900 --> 00:24:38.900
You don't understand.

00:24:38.900 --> 00:24:41.900
And what about the district attorney and the jury?

00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:44.900
Each one of them is an executioner.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:47.900
Please, Chief, a man is going to die because I...

00:24:47.900 --> 00:24:51.900
If he does, if he does die,

00:24:51.900 --> 00:24:56.900
you won't have killed him, Miss Whitfield, any more than I or the DA or the jury.

00:24:57.900 --> 00:25:00.900
His punishment is fixed by the laws of this state.

00:25:00.900 --> 00:25:03.900
But they're wrong. Barbaric.

00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:05.900
Then change them.

00:25:05.900 --> 00:25:09.900
But you can't change your responsibility as a citizen.

00:25:09.900 --> 00:25:12.900
When a crime is committed, it's your duty to report the facts.

00:25:12.900 --> 00:25:15.900
It's easy for you to talk. You're a policeman.

00:25:15.900 --> 00:25:18.900
This is all just... just routine.

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:22.900
The day murder and execution are just routine.

00:25:22.900 --> 00:25:25.900
I'll walk out of this office.

00:25:29.900 --> 00:25:33.900
Did you ever consider the other side of the coin, Miss Whitfield?

00:25:34.900 --> 00:25:39.900
Every time one man is proven guilty, ten others are proven innocent.

00:25:39.900 --> 00:25:41.900
You're right.

00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:45.900
You do have a big mouth.

00:25:45.900 --> 00:25:48.900
And it says some big words.

00:25:49.900 --> 00:25:51.900
Just doing some missionary work.

00:25:51.900 --> 00:25:53.900
Trying to gain a convert.

00:25:53.900 --> 00:25:55.900
Me?

00:25:55.900 --> 00:25:57.900
Speaking philosophically, of course.

00:25:57.900 --> 00:26:15.900
What kind of a future could the police department offer a woman like you?

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:29.900
I'm sorry.

00:26:52.900 --> 00:26:56.900
Pawnbroker sure didn't take Kessel's address and the gun permit number for nothing,

00:26:56.900 --> 00:26:58.900
but he's a nice sharkie.

00:26:58.900 --> 00:27:02.900
He just came from the east. Has a record of working alone.

00:27:07.900 --> 00:27:09.900
Chief, you with me?

00:27:09.900 --> 00:27:28.900
I'm with you.

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:33.900
Hello, Chief.

00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:36.900
Well, Miss Whitfield, it's been a long time.

00:27:36.900 --> 00:27:38.900
On your way to another important case?

00:27:38.900 --> 00:27:40.900
Just finished a lecture at the police academy.

00:27:40.900 --> 00:27:42.900
More missionary work?

00:27:42.900 --> 00:27:44.900
Part of my job.

00:27:44.900 --> 00:27:46.900
How about lunch?

00:27:46.900 --> 00:27:47.900
I'm sorry, I...

00:27:47.900 --> 00:27:50.900
Come on, you haven't finished converting me.

00:27:51.900 --> 00:27:53.900
Miss Whitfield, I...

00:27:56.900 --> 00:27:58.900
HCOs, next block, take a right.

00:27:58.900 --> 00:28:01.900
Unless you're too chicken to let a woman buy your lunch.

00:28:01.900 --> 00:28:03.900
Wait a minute.

00:28:03.900 --> 00:28:05.900
What's the matter? Don't we have any colors you like?

00:28:05.900 --> 00:28:06.900
What's that?

00:28:06.900 --> 00:28:09.900
Oh, sorry, Chief. What's the trouble? Anything I can do?

00:28:09.900 --> 00:28:11.900
Yes.

00:28:11.900 --> 00:28:14.900
We've got an anti-noise ordinance in this town, don't we?

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:16.900
Yes, sir.

00:28:19.900 --> 00:28:22.900
Come on, get this going. Hurry up. Hey!

00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:26.900
Well, now, taking a little time out, isn't that painful, is it?

00:28:26.900 --> 00:28:28.900
Of course not.

00:28:28.900 --> 00:28:30.900
It's very pleasant, in fact.

00:28:30.900 --> 00:28:32.900
It's good to see you again.

00:28:32.900 --> 00:28:34.900
Thank you. And you.

00:28:35.900 --> 00:28:39.900
You know, I always wanted to talk to you about that first night we met.

00:28:39.900 --> 00:28:41.900
I never had a chance to explain.

00:28:41.900 --> 00:28:43.900
Explain what?

00:28:43.900 --> 00:28:45.900
I mean, I don't know.

00:28:45.900 --> 00:28:47.900
I mean, I don't know what you're talking about.

00:28:47.900 --> 00:28:49.900
I mean, I don't know what you're talking about.

00:28:49.900 --> 00:28:52.900
I never had a chance to explain.

00:28:52.900 --> 00:28:54.900
Explain what?

00:28:54.900 --> 00:28:57.900
What we... Paul and I...

00:28:57.900 --> 00:28:59.900
We weren't in that place...

00:28:59.900 --> 00:29:02.900
well, like you thought.

00:29:02.900 --> 00:29:04.900
Islam-ing was your word.

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:06.900
It was stupid.

00:29:06.900 --> 00:29:09.900
There was a new trio playing, and I wanted to hear them.

00:29:09.900 --> 00:29:12.900
I thought perhaps they could play at our fashion show.

00:29:12.900 --> 00:29:14.900
And...

00:29:14.900 --> 00:29:16.900
well...

00:29:16.900 --> 00:29:19.900
why am I apologizing to you?

00:29:19.900 --> 00:29:22.900
I don't know. Why are you?

00:29:22.900 --> 00:29:26.900
Oh, I suppose I'm a little ashamed.

00:29:26.900 --> 00:29:29.900
Trying to change your impression of me.

00:29:29.900 --> 00:29:31.900
What's my impression?

00:29:31.900 --> 00:29:34.900
Usual. Rich. Scatterbrained.

00:29:34.900 --> 00:29:36.900
Useless.

00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:38.900
Scatterbrained? No.

00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:41.900
Rich? Yes, but don't knock it.

00:29:41.900 --> 00:29:43.900
Useless?

00:29:43.900 --> 00:29:46.900
Well, you're pretty good at selling raffle tickets.

00:29:46.900 --> 00:29:48.900
And riding and sailing,

00:29:48.900 --> 00:29:51.900
throwing parties, visiting art galleries,

00:29:51.900 --> 00:29:55.900
taking trips, everything the proper little society girl's supposed to do.

00:29:55.900 --> 00:29:58.900
Miss Whitfield, if you expect me to feel sorry for you...

00:29:58.900 --> 00:30:01.900
No. Please don't patronize me.

00:30:02.900 --> 00:30:05.900
Well, if I have, I apologize.

00:30:09.900 --> 00:30:12.900
Couldn't you just hear the violins?

00:30:12.900 --> 00:30:14.900
Poor butterfly.

00:30:15.900 --> 00:30:19.900
You know, there's nothing wrong with you that a nice, steady...

00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:21.900
Now you sound like my parents.

00:30:21.900 --> 00:30:25.900
There's nothing wrong with you that a nice, steady husband wouldn't cure.

00:30:25.900 --> 00:30:28.900
I was about to suggest a job.

00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:30.900
Like what?

00:30:30.900 --> 00:30:32.900
Depends on your qualifications.

00:30:32.900 --> 00:30:37.900
Riding, sailing, taking trips, visiting art galleries?

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:39.900
Poor butterfly.

00:30:39.900 --> 00:30:41.900
Well, honestly, there's very little I can do.

00:30:41.900 --> 00:30:43.900
Well, then learn.

00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.900
Go back to school, if necessary.

00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:48.900
You'll find something if you really want to.

00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:50.900
You almost make me believe it.

00:30:50.900 --> 00:30:52.900
But not quite.

00:30:52.900 --> 00:30:54.900
Enough to give it a try.

00:30:54.900 --> 00:30:56.900
All right.

00:30:56.900 --> 00:31:00.900
To the new Eve Whitfield, career woman.

00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:03.900
And that's another decision.

00:31:05.900 --> 00:31:08.900
Well, I'm afraid I have to go.

00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:10.900
Whatever.

00:31:11.900 --> 00:31:13.900
It'll be a success.

00:31:13.900 --> 00:31:15.900
Chief Ironside.

00:31:18.900 --> 00:31:20.900
You better knock on wood.

00:31:23.900 --> 00:31:24.900
Who is it?

00:31:24.900 --> 00:31:26.900
Police.

00:31:31.900 --> 00:31:32.900
Yes?

00:31:32.900 --> 00:31:35.900
I'm Sergeant Brown. This is Chief Ironside.

00:31:35.900 --> 00:31:37.900
What do you want?

00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:39.900
We're looking for Fred Kessel.

00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:41.900
Come on. My husband's dead.

00:31:41.900 --> 00:31:43.900
More than a year now.

00:31:44.900 --> 00:31:46.900
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

00:31:46.900 --> 00:32:06.900
Mrs. Kessel, we want some information. Perhaps you could help us.

00:32:10.900 --> 00:32:12.900
Well?

00:32:12.900 --> 00:32:16.900
Did your husband own a gun, Mrs. Kessel?

00:32:16.900 --> 00:32:18.900
He was a bank messenger.

00:32:18.900 --> 00:32:20.900
Then he had a gun permit.

00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:22.900
Sure, he had to.

00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:24.900
What happened to the gun permit?

00:32:24.900 --> 00:32:26.900
I don't know.

00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:29.900
Did you save any of your husband's personal papers?

00:32:29.900 --> 00:32:30.900
Yeah.

00:32:30.900 --> 00:32:33.900
You know, usual stuff.

00:32:33.900 --> 00:32:35.900
Kind of like keepsakes.

00:32:35.900 --> 00:32:42.900
Would you please check them?

00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:44.900
What's this all about, anyway?

00:32:44.900 --> 00:32:49.900
The owner of a pawn shop on 4th Street was shot and killed this morning.

00:32:49.900 --> 00:32:55.900
Sometime before that, he made a record of your husband's name and a number of his gun permit.

00:32:55.900 --> 00:32:57.900
That's crazy.

00:32:57.900 --> 00:33:00.900
There may be some reasonable explanation.

00:33:00.900 --> 00:33:05.900
But first we have to find that permit.

00:34:01.900 --> 00:34:29.900
I'm sorry. I just can't find it.

00:34:29.900 --> 00:34:34.900
Mrs. Kessel, does the name Frank Sharkey mean anything to you?

00:34:34.900 --> 00:34:36.900
Frank Sh...

00:34:36.900 --> 00:34:37.900
Sharkey.

00:34:37.900 --> 00:34:41.900
Yeah. I know him. I've seen him a couple of times.

00:34:41.900 --> 00:34:43.900
That's all?

00:34:43.900 --> 00:34:45.900
That's all.

00:34:45.900 --> 00:34:50.900
Well, can you tell us anything about him?

00:34:50.900 --> 00:34:53.900
Just a man. Why?

00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:57.900
We believe he's the man who shot the pawnbroker.

00:34:57.900 --> 00:34:59.900
Now, when did you see him last?

00:34:59.900 --> 00:35:02.900
A couple of weeks ago.

00:35:02.900 --> 00:35:04.900
I don't remember.

00:35:04.900 --> 00:35:16.900
All right, Mrs. Kessel. Thank you for your help.

00:35:16.900 --> 00:35:21.900
Mrs. Kessel, we've assumed...

00:35:21.900 --> 00:35:25.900
perhaps we've been presumptuous.

00:35:25.900 --> 00:35:27.900
But you haven't remarried.

00:35:27.900 --> 00:35:37.900
No.

00:35:37.900 --> 00:35:39.900
Anything more you'd like to know?

00:35:39.900 --> 00:35:41.900
Not now.

00:35:41.900 --> 00:35:49.900
Sorry to have bothered you, Mrs. Kessel.

00:35:49.900 --> 00:35:52.900
I'm ready to bet that Sharkey stole that gun permit.

00:35:52.900 --> 00:35:57.900
He still may be involved with Kessel's widow, so hold that stakeout around the clock.

00:35:57.900 --> 00:36:16.900
If anything breaks, you can reach Ed or me at the hospital.

00:36:16.900 --> 00:36:18.900
Third floor, Miss Kiley.

00:36:18.900 --> 00:36:21.900
Yes, he's here.

00:36:21.900 --> 00:36:23.900
I'll tell him.

00:36:23.900 --> 00:36:25.900
That was the operating room, Mr. Sanger.

00:36:25.900 --> 00:36:27.900
Miss Whitfield is still in surgery.

00:36:27.900 --> 00:36:29.900
She's doing as well as can be expected.

00:36:29.900 --> 00:36:31.900
What's that supposed to mean?

00:36:31.900 --> 00:36:33.900
I'm sorry, Mr. Sanger.

00:36:33.900 --> 00:37:01.900
There's nothing more I can tell you.

00:37:01.900 --> 00:37:03.900
You're making me nervous.

00:37:03.900 --> 00:37:05.900
Why don't you take a walk?

00:37:05.900 --> 00:37:08.900
Go get yourself some supper. You haven't eaten yet.

00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:12.900
Mark's getting some sandwiches.

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:14.900
Hello.

00:37:14.900 --> 00:37:17.900
Yes, he's here. Who's calling, please?

00:37:17.900 --> 00:37:21.900
Just a minute. Mrs. Kessel.

00:37:21.900 --> 00:37:23.900
This is Ironside.

00:37:23.900 --> 00:37:25.900
I...

00:37:25.900 --> 00:37:27.900
I...

00:37:27.900 --> 00:37:29.900
Mrs. Kessel, I can't hear you.

00:37:29.900 --> 00:37:33.900
The man you're looking for, he was here.

00:37:33.900 --> 00:37:36.900
Frank Sharkey? When?

00:37:36.900 --> 00:37:38.900
A little while ago.

00:37:38.900 --> 00:37:40.900
It was terrible.

00:37:40.900 --> 00:37:43.900
Sharkey was just there. Check the stakeout.

00:37:43.900 --> 00:37:46.900
Yes, Mrs. Kessel.

00:37:46.900 --> 00:37:49.900
Try to control yourself.

00:37:49.900 --> 00:37:51.900
When...

00:37:51.900 --> 00:37:55.900
When I told him that you'd been here, he got so mad.

00:37:55.900 --> 00:37:59.900
Mrs. Kessel, do you know where he went?

00:37:59.900 --> 00:38:01.900
Did he give you any idea?

00:38:01.900 --> 00:38:03.900
No.

00:38:03.900 --> 00:38:05.900
He took all my money.

00:38:05.900 --> 00:38:09.900
Fred's old driver's license.

00:38:09.900 --> 00:38:11.900
Yes.

00:38:11.900 --> 00:38:13.900
He knew just where it was.

00:38:13.900 --> 00:38:16.900
Then he could have taken that gun permit, too.

00:38:16.900 --> 00:38:18.900
Yes.

00:38:18.900 --> 00:38:20.900
Oh, please.

00:38:20.900 --> 00:38:24.900
Please, try to understand.

00:38:24.900 --> 00:38:26.900
I've been so lonely.

00:38:26.900 --> 00:38:28.900
Mrs. Kessel.

00:38:38.900 --> 00:38:42.900
I never saw him. I figure he must have gone across the rooves.

00:38:42.900 --> 00:38:44.900
Query.

00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:47.900
Why did Sharkey take Kessel's old driver's license?

00:38:47.900 --> 00:38:49.900
Did he?

00:38:49.900 --> 00:38:51.900
Must have needed it to drive a car.

00:38:51.900 --> 00:38:54.900
Query. What car? His own?

00:38:54.900 --> 00:38:56.900
Then he would have had a driver's license,

00:38:56.900 --> 00:38:59.900
and we'd have had a record of it, plus the car registration.

00:38:59.900 --> 00:39:01.900
Maybe he figures on stealing one.

00:39:01.900 --> 00:39:03.900
Pin another warning sign on himself,

00:39:03.900 --> 00:39:06.900
so we'd also be looking for a hot car?

00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:09.900
Besides, why worry about the legality

00:39:09.900 --> 00:39:11.900
of a driver's license at that point?

00:39:11.900 --> 00:39:14.900
You're leading up to your own answer.

00:39:14.900 --> 00:39:17.900
Outside of buying a car, which is highly unlikely,

00:39:17.900 --> 00:39:21.900
how else can you get one and have to show identification?

00:39:21.900 --> 00:39:23.900
Rental. Get on it.

00:39:23.900 --> 00:39:26.900
Cover the downtown agencies first and work out.

00:39:26.900 --> 00:39:29.900
Ed.

00:39:29.900 --> 00:39:33.900
If this thing pans out, bring Sharkey in.

00:39:33.900 --> 00:39:47.900
I want him alive.

00:39:47.900 --> 00:39:49.900
Where do you think you're...

00:39:49.900 --> 00:39:52.900
Oh, it's you.

00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:54.900
Do you mind?

00:39:54.900 --> 00:39:56.900
What's the big rush?

00:39:56.900 --> 00:39:59.900
Traffic detail spotted Howie Regal. He's holed up in a loft.

00:39:59.900 --> 00:40:01.900
Regal? The men who shot your partner?

00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:03.900
That's right.

00:40:03.900 --> 00:40:05.900
But this isn't your case, is it?

00:40:05.900 --> 00:40:10.900
He killed my partner.

00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:12.900
Oh, no, Ed.

00:40:12.900 --> 00:40:13.900
Eve, I'm in a hurry.

00:40:13.900 --> 00:40:17.900
To do what? Arrest a man or to kill him?

00:40:17.900 --> 00:40:21.900
Listen, rookie, don't let that shiny new badge go to your head.

00:40:21.900 --> 00:40:24.900
I'm sorry. I don't mean to be telling you what to do,

00:40:24.900 --> 00:40:27.900
but I'm only learning some of the things you've probably forgotten,

00:40:27.900 --> 00:40:31.900
like what people always think happens to a cop killer.

00:40:31.900 --> 00:40:34.900
An automatic death sentence. That's what everyone believes.

00:40:34.900 --> 00:40:36.900
The police always take care of their own first,

00:40:36.900 --> 00:40:40.900
and when something happens to one of them, they pay back double.

00:40:40.900 --> 00:40:43.900
They don't want justice. They want vengeance.

00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:47.900
That's a lie.

00:40:47.900 --> 00:41:14.900
Are you sure?

00:41:14.900 --> 00:41:15.900
Mobile 25, Brown.

00:41:15.900 --> 00:41:18.900
This is Bonero. Talk about timing.

00:41:18.900 --> 00:41:20.900
One of the car rental agencies we're calling?

00:41:20.900 --> 00:41:23.900
Sharky's there right now.

00:41:23.900 --> 00:41:24.900
Uh-huh.

00:41:24.900 --> 00:41:28.900
Showed Kessel's driver's license for identification.

00:41:28.900 --> 00:41:31.900
Clerk said he tried to stall him.

00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:34.900
Zeno rental on Mason.

00:41:34.900 --> 00:41:36.900
Got it. I'm only a few blocks from there.

00:41:36.900 --> 00:41:53.900
You pull in the men.

00:41:53.900 --> 00:41:54.900
Sergeant Brown, you reported a...

00:41:54.900 --> 00:41:56.900
He just went upstairs. I couldn't stall him any longer.

00:41:56.900 --> 00:41:57.900
Upstairs where?

00:41:57.900 --> 00:42:00.900
Second level. I gave him that blue four-door near the inn.

00:42:00.900 --> 00:42:01.900
Okay, keep everybody off that level.

00:42:01.900 --> 00:42:30.900
I'm going to be here any minute.

00:42:30.900 --> 00:42:54.900
Hold it, Sharky! Police!

00:42:54.900 --> 00:43:07.900
Basic car! Put your hands on the roof!

00:43:07.900 --> 00:43:36.900
Right there.

00:43:36.900 --> 00:43:38.900
Okay?

00:43:38.900 --> 00:43:43.900
Don't move.

00:43:43.900 --> 00:43:57.900
All right, all right, don't shoot.

00:43:57.900 --> 00:44:18.900
Don't shoot.

00:44:18.900 --> 00:44:20.900
No one hurt.

00:44:20.900 --> 00:44:23.900
Good work. Stay on it.

00:44:23.900 --> 00:44:25.900
Chief Ironside?

00:44:25.900 --> 00:44:26.900
Yes?

00:44:26.900 --> 00:44:28.900
Good afternoon.

00:44:28.900 --> 00:44:30.900
Well, hello.

00:44:30.900 --> 00:44:35.900
Sorry to disturb you, but it'll only take a minute.

00:44:35.900 --> 00:44:38.900
I need your signature.

00:44:38.900 --> 00:44:40.900
Police again?

00:44:40.900 --> 00:44:45.900
I took the liberty of saying that you'd recommend me.

00:44:45.900 --> 00:44:49.900
Miss Whitfield, are you sure you know what you're doing?

00:44:49.900 --> 00:44:53.900
There you go. Sounding like my parents again.

00:44:53.900 --> 00:44:56.900
No, I don't. It's absolutely insane.

00:44:56.900 --> 00:45:00.900
But I want to try it anyway.

00:45:00.900 --> 00:45:02.900
Fair enough.

00:45:02.900 --> 00:45:06.900
There's room at the bottom for personal remarks if you'd like to add any.

00:45:06.900 --> 00:45:07.900
I can think of a few.

00:45:07.900 --> 00:45:10.900
That would help me.

00:45:10.900 --> 00:45:33.900
I'll try.

00:45:33.900 --> 00:45:34.900
Are you looking for somebody?

00:45:34.900 --> 00:45:36.900
Mm-hmm.

00:45:36.900 --> 00:45:40.900
These your stake-ins?

00:45:40.900 --> 00:45:42.900
Outs.

00:45:42.900 --> 00:45:44.900
Stake-outs.

00:45:44.900 --> 00:45:52.900
Oh.

00:45:52.900 --> 00:45:54.900
All right, Miss Whitfield.

00:45:54.900 --> 00:45:59.900
Your application for blood, sweat, and tears.

00:45:59.900 --> 00:46:02.900
Conscientious. Dedicated.

00:46:02.900 --> 00:46:07.900
Those are lovely words.

00:46:07.900 --> 00:46:09.900
I hope I can live up to them.

00:46:09.900 --> 00:46:11.900
You'd better.

00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:13.900
Nobody makes a liar out of me.

00:46:13.900 --> 00:46:15.900
Come in, come in.

00:46:15.900 --> 00:46:17.900
Chief, I'm inside.

00:46:17.900 --> 00:46:19.900
I just had a call from surgery.

00:46:19.900 --> 00:46:27.900
I wanted you to know right away.

00:46:27.900 --> 00:46:33.900
Thank you, nurse.

00:46:33.900 --> 00:46:41.900
And I hereby certify that the aforesaid officer is physically fit to return to active duty, signed J.L. Travis, Medical Department, San Francisco Police.

00:46:41.900 --> 00:46:47.900
All you have to do is countersign it and I'm back in harness.

00:46:47.900 --> 00:46:49.900
Well?

00:46:49.900 --> 00:46:54.900
Can't help thinking if I hadn't signed another paper like this, you'd never have been shot.

00:46:54.900 --> 00:46:59.900
No. I'd have broken my neck fox hunting or drowned while sailing.

00:46:59.900 --> 00:47:01.900
There are no guarantees.

00:47:01.900 --> 00:47:09.900
Let me live my life at least.

00:47:09.900 --> 00:47:12.900
Last chance to back out.

00:47:12.900 --> 00:47:18.900
It is my life.

00:47:18.900 --> 00:47:26.900
All right, everybody.

00:47:26.900 --> 00:47:28.900
Chow down.

00:47:28.900 --> 00:47:31.900
Your birthday present.

00:47:31.900 --> 00:47:34.900
You couldn't have thought of anything more appropriate, Eve.

00:47:34.900 --> 00:47:49.900
I guess the only kind of pot a chili won't burn a hole through.

00:48:04.900 --> 00:48:24.900
